IceWM: put the taskbar on RandR's primary output

Without a XineramaPrimaryScreenName preference IceWM takes the first monitor
in its own list as the primary one, and that list reorders whenever a monitor
changes (xrandr --rotate, --mode): the taskbar then jumps to another monitor.
Use the server's primary output instead, which xrandr --primary sets.

--- a/src/ywindow.cc	2026-10-13 07:50:51.396490042 +0000
+++ b/src/ywindow.cc	2026-10-13 07:50:51.413983606 +0000
@@ -2028,6 +2028,17 @@
                 XRRFreeOutputInfo(oinfo);
             }
         }
+        else if (xrrsr) {
+            /* no XineramaPrimaryScreenName: the server's primary output
+               (xrandr --primary) */
+            RROutput primary = XRRGetOutputPrimary(xapp->display(), handle());
+            XRROutputInfo *oinfo = primary ?
+                XRRGetOutputInfo(xapp->display(), xrrsr, primary) : nullptr;
+            if (oinfo) {
+                primaryCRT = oinfo->crtc;
+                XRRFreeOutputInfo(oinfo);
+            }
+        }
 
         for (int i = 0; xrrsr && i < xrrsr->ncrtc; i++) {
             XRRCrtcInfo *ci = XRRGetCrtcInfo(xapp->display(), xrrsr,
